Description: censorship-resistant zero-upstream DNS resolver and bypass stack
 A self-hosted recursive DNS resolver and censorship-bypass stack, built from
 source with no upstream forwarders and no black-box binaries.
 .
 The resolver resolves from the root hints downward on its own. On a
 censored network, where UDP/53 answers are forged, a second tier reaches
 authoritative servers over DoH on HTTPS/443 and cross-checks the result,
 rejecting injected private-address answers.
 .
 Also included: DNS-over-TLS and DNS-over-HTTPS front ends, DPI desync
 bypass (zapret nfqws/tpws and ciadpi), Tor transport, Web3/ENS and
 gaming-DNS resolvers, an intrusion-detection daemon, a self-healing
 watchdog, and web dashboards for the whole stack.
 .
 Every feature is independently switchable at runtime from the dashboard
 control plane, which is protected by a token stored outside the source
 tree.